concept :the_lodged_half do
  name "The Lodged Half"
  aka "the counter-draw", "存證"
  tags :trade, :legibility, :legitimacy, :biotech
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    An article that changes hands between the connected and the unconnected worlds is drawn in two. One half goes to the buyer; the matched half is sealed at the same bench in the same hour and lodged with a house that trades in neither biology nor computation. The house enters it in a numbering book, hands the depositor a counterfoil, and holds it for #{duration 1} from the day of receipt. A complaint filed inside the term is decided against the lodged half, and the trade calls the lodged half 存證 — deposited evidence.

    What a half is depends on the article. Living stock is a slip of tissue off the same flush, sealed damp in a tinned copper tube. A model is a copy written to #{ref :witness_glass, "witness glass"} from the same source in the same hour as the copy that ships. #{ref :the_brokers, "The Pearl River houses"} draw against every interface they build to order, and the workshops buying from them draw against whatever they pay with.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :mechanics, heading: "The Term And The Two Tiers"
    The term runs from the day the lodging house receipts the half, not from the day the article reaches the buyer. A half that crosses slowly spends the buyer's protection on the road, so halves travel by the fastest carrier available and by a different route from the goods they answer for. #{ref :wing_lok_godown, "Wing Lok"} prints both dates on one line of the receipt.

    A depositor buys certification at lodging, in one of two tiers. The lower tier is the seal: the house states that the tube was sound or that the block's top leaf was unmarked when it came in, and will state it again on any day of the term. The upper tier is the article itself — a flush raised off the tissue slip and put in front of the house's test plate, witnessed and entered. Living stock can be had at either tier. A model can only be had at the lower one, because the only way to establish what is on a block of witness glass is to separate it, and a separated block is no longer lodged with anybody.

    Opening is on proof and not on suspicion. The complainant names the defect, gives the day it appeared, and brings the article to the house; the half stays in its room until the bench has all three.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "What A Half Proves"
    A lodged half documents the article on the day of the draw. The #{ref :the_gatekeepers, "Gatekeepers"} price a lineage audit lower against an unbroken lodging receipt and enter the receipt on the audit as part of the lineage; the godowns print the day of the draw on the face of the receipt and nothing earlier, and a house that has drawn against the same #{ref :severed_strains, "severed strain"} at every sale it has ever made can produce a shelf of receipts and no ancestry.

    At the close of the term the tissue is autoclaved, the glass is crushed, and the destruction is entered on the same line as the receipt. Nothing survives the term. A fault that takes longer than the term to show belongs to whoever is holding the article when it shows, which is why buyers of #{ref :feral_models, "ferals"} across the line argue for a longer term at every draw and pay by the month for the rooms when they get one.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The term, the receipt-dated clock and the sealing rule come from seed-lot referee sampling, a trade nobody in the godowns practises: a testing house keeps a retained sample for not less than a year after receipt, and a sample that passes through unauthorised hands must be sealed so that tampering shows. Borrowed because it puts the argument in a date printed on a receipt instead of either party's word, and starting the clock at receipt rather than delivery gives the trade its own reason to move a half faster than the goods."
  log "2026-08-09 — The two tiers, and opening only on proof of a named and dated defect, come from source-code escrow: a neutral agent holds the deposit, will certify at tiers from an intact-seal statement up to building and running what was deposited, and releases only when the claimant shows the triggering condition. Borrowed because it makes verification something bought at the draw rather than argued afterwards, and because the tiers fall unevenly on the two civilizations' articles — a fungal half can be tested and a model half cannot."
end
